    "profile_categories": "Disjoint self-time partition of every pstats function. All warnings.py self time plus immediate callees self time on pstats caller edges assigned to warnings; subtract those edges before classifying remaining function self time. Conversion bucket is dumper convert_var_to_dict, safe_getattr, and attribute-name listcomp own self time. Type-check bucket is isinstance, issubclass, and __instancecheck__ remaining self time. Attribute bucket is dir/getattr/startswith remaining self time. JSON bucket is json module functions, orjson.dumps, dumper serialize/_json_default remaining self time, including serializability probes. Everything else is residual. Sum checked against pstats total. This is a profiled CPU main-thread partition, not a measured partition of ordinary-run added overhead.",
    "trace_counts": "Every raw pre record counted once; records kept in original order, grouped using exact step metadata and exact call IDs. Serialized variables counted by original singleton type-tag dictionaries in args, kwargs and return_values. Snapshot counts count repeated observations, not unique objects.",
    "regions": "Regions only label call counts, not timings. For each step, zero-grad region extends through matching zero_grad post. Forward extends until nll_loss pre. Loss extends until Tensor.backward pre. Backward extends through matching backward post. Everything after is update/gradient processing. Nested call counts are included. These regions do not measure device kernels."
